. She is the former leader and main rapper of the girl group AOA and guitarist of the sub-unit AOA Black, which debuted under FNC Entertainment. In 2015, Jimin was a semi-finalist in the first season of Unpretty Rapstar. During the show, she released several successful collaboration singles, most notably \"Good Start\" (with Seulong) and \"Puss\" (with Iron). Following allegations of bullying by former bandmate Kwon Mina, Jimin left the group and retired from the entertainment industry in July 2020. She returned to the entertainment industry in July 2022.","title":"Shin Ji-min","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shin_Ji-min"}},"Q16184245":{"id":"Q16184245","name":"Hyoeun","ko":"효은","birthName":"이효은","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Hyo-eun"],"birth":"1993-03-16","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q12603717","name":"Stellar","start":"2012","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/hyonile_e/","x":"https://x.com/hyoni_0316_","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/58d278dc-ca47-41ca-812b-7a615d41ac92"},"photo":null,"bio":null,"positions":["Main vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%ED%9A%A8%EC%9D%80"}}},"Q169717":{"id":"Q169717","name":"Kim Jae-joong","ko":"김재중","birthName":"한재준","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Jae-jung","Hero Jae-joong","Han Jae-joon","Kim Jejung","Gim Jae-jung","Jejung","Jaejoong","Hero Jaejoong"],"birth":"1986-01-26","death":"","birthplace":"Gongju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["television actor","singer","film actor","singer-songwriter","actor","model"],"debut":"2003","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""},{"name":"C-JeS Studios","korean":true,"id":"Q5005884","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Rhythm Zone","korean":false,"id":"Q1154245","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q192983","name":"TVXQ","start":"2003","end":"2009"},{"id":"Q51729","name":"JYJ","start":"2010","end":""}],"links":{"website":"https://www.in-kode.com/kim_jaejoong.html","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jj_1986_jj/","x":"https://x.com/bornfreeonekiss","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCkDL3JYoQIZAq-CdPMoPXwQ","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/2x4LoC3la2S3aUHxaP8w1T","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/46d72c85-ba81-4d50-bb6e-5d628dc08d55"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Jae-joong, also known mononymously as Jaejoong in South Korea and Jejung/J-Jun (ジェジュン) in Japan, is a South Korean singer-songwriter, actor and director. He is a member of the Korean duo JX, a former member of JYJ and was one of the original members of boy band TVXQ!, where he was formerly known by the stage name Hero Jae-joong (영웅재중). Since 2013, he has expanded his range of activities as a solo artist, and in 2023, he formed his own agency Inkode, where he serves as the Chief Strategy Officer. Born in Gongju, South Chungcheong Province, he moved to Seoul as a teenager to audition for SM Entertainment. From 2003 to 2010, he was the lead vocalist of South Korean boy band TVXQ.","title":"Kim Jae-joong","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Jae-joong"},"positions":["Main vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EA%B9%80%EC%9E%AC%EC%A4%91"}}},"Q20944949":{"id":"Q20944949","name":"Na Ha-eun","ko":"나하은","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"2009-01-16","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","dancer"],"debut":"2026","agencies":[{"name":"High Up Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q101434470"