irst made her debut as a child actress, appearing as a supporting cast member on the SBS historical drama Ballad of Seodong (2005). Following this, she earned a number of guest roles, appearing in the television series Love Needs a Miracle (2005) and Drama City (2007), and the film Vacation (2006). She then subsequently appeared in the independent films Punch Lady (2007) and BA:BO (2008), the former being her first time cast in a substantial dramatic role. After signing a record deal with SM Entertainment, Sulli rose to prominence as a member of the girl group f(x) formed in 2009.","title":"Sulli","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulli"},"mbti":"ENFP","factSources":{"mbti":{"name":"Kpop Wiki","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","base":"https://kpop.fandom.com/wiki/","url":"https://kpop.fandom.com/wiki/Sulli"}}},"Q498805":{"id":"Q498805","name":"Bada","ko":"바다","birthName":"Choi Sung-hee","birthNameEn":"Choi Sung-hee","aliases":["Choi Sung-hee","Sea"],"birth":"1980-02-28","death":"","birthplace":"Bucheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","composer"],"debut":"1997","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q491542","name":"S.E.S.","start":"2016","end":"2017"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/bada0228/","x":"https://x.com/Bada0228","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC0D7tPBhxeFxNDUrrT4JBcw","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/9e585ff3-3dc1-44e1-88d4-35fb451d7da6"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Choi Sung-hee, known professionally as Bada (바다) (also known as Sea), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, composer, musical actress and television presenter. She debuted as a member of the South Korean girl group S.E.S. in 1997, which went on to become one of the best-selling artists in South Korea. After S.E.S. disbanded in December 2002, she released her first solo studio album, A Day of Renew, in October 2003. Since then, she continued her active singing career with songs such as Aurora, Eyes, V.I.P, GoGoGo, Queen, and Mad.","title":"Bada (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bada_%28singer%29"}},"Q5372469":{"id":"Q5372469","name":"Kim E-Z","ko":"김이지","birthName":"Kim Ei-ji","birthNameEn":"Kim Ei-ji","aliases":["Kim EZ","Kim Ei-ji","Kim Eiji","Kim Ei Ji","EZ Kim","Kim Hee-jung"],"birth":"1979-01-31","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"1997","agencies":[{"name":"DR Music","korean":true,"id":"Q17008158","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q490213","name":"Baby V.O.X.","start":"2024","end":"2006"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/ezez0417/","x":"https://x.com/briller0417","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/7c623e5b-8f68-443e-a8f2-40a9c8b98fa2"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Hee-jung, better known as Kim E-Z (김이지), is a South Korean singer, rapper, actress and television host and a member of the Korean girl group Baby V.O.X.","title":"Kim E-Z","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_E-Z"},"positions":["Leader","Sub vocalist","Main rapper"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EA%B9%80%EC%9D%B4%EC%A7%80"}}},"Q56824821":{"id":"Q56824821","name":"Yeojin","ko":"여진 (2002년)","birthName":"Im Yeo-jin","birthNameEn":"Im Yeo-jin","aliases":["YeoJin","Im Yeo-jin"],"birth":"2002-11-11","death":"","birthplace":"Daegu","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2017","agencies":[{"name":"Blockberry Creative","korean":true,"id":"Q48989772","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q28025953","name":"Loona","start":"2017","end":"2023"},{"id":"Q121975741","name":"Loossemble","start":"2023","end":"2024"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yeo